Impacts on biodiversity
2.1. What do we mean by biodiversity?
Biodiversity refers to the biological variety of all life on earth or within certain habitats.11 An ecosystem refers to the interaction of organisms within certain habitats.12 This review focuses on the impact of ammonia emissions on biodiversity, recognising that biodiversity is a vital component of healthy and functioning ecosystems. Box 1 outlines the common measures of biodiversity.
2.2. Why is biodiversity important?
