2. To collect evidence to support policymaking relating to the air quality strategy and post-Brexit future of the countryside discussions.
The work will be conducted over the next 3 months and the outcomes of the study will be made publicly available and disseminated among policymakers by the Royal Society during summer 2018.
As part of the project, we are conducting key informant interviews with experts on the topic to test our understanding, ensure we have identified key literature and also supplement our search with unpublished data or relevant sources beyond academic journal articles.
The project will be written up as a public report which will be available on Royal Society and RAND websites, and should be completed by late summer 2018.
